db/ref 1072 #uuid "5ade80e9-fb10-5f67-9c65-ab5d8d98adbc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351158 #edb/ref 1074 "To find every subset of $U,$ we list out every combination of elements within $U.$ \n\nWe can use the following diagram to visualize the process:\n\n![](images/b0/b0e483a2d10cba17fb2bd3bf0e78d7b4d2fc07b22dbb5c492564b998bbfce6fc.png)\n\nNote that we must include the empty set since it is a subset of every set.\n\nBy doing this, we get\n\n$$\n∅,{-\\pi },{\\pi },{-\\pi ,\\pi }.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351176 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186351004 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351176 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80876" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351176 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351176 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $C$  be the set of all multiples of $10$ greater than $0$ and let $D$  be the the set of all multiples of $5$ greater than $0.$ What is $C∖D?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351176 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1076728a-78e3-5cde-ae2f-0952fd39a682" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351176 #edb/ref 1074 "The multiples of $10$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nC={10,20,30,40,50,60,70,…}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $5$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nD={5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,45,50,55,60,65,70,75,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, $C∖D$ is the *difference* of $C$ and $D,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $C$ but *not* in $D.$\n\nThe elements of $C$ that are also in $D$ are $10,20,30,40,$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $10$). So, we must remove these elements from $C.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C∖D & =C-D \\\\  & ={10,20,30,40,50,60,70,…}-{5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,45,50,55,60,65,70,75,…} \\\\  & =∅.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351258 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186350765 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351258 #edb/ref 1069 "q-81203" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351258 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351258 #edb/ref 1071 "If $U={1,2,3,…,10}$ is the universal set and $A={2,4,6,8,10},$ then the complement of $A$ is" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351258 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "35334f88-cecb-5c05-827d-5c2f77f4118a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351258 #edb/ref 1074 "The complement of $A,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{A},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $A.$\n\nThe elements of $U$ that are not in $A$ are $1,$ $3,$ $5,$ $7,$ and $9.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $A$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{A}={1,3,5,7,9}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351259 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186350983 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351259 #edb/ref 1069 "q-81205" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351259 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351259 #edb/ref 1071 "If $U={-20,-18,-16,-14,…,20}$ is the universal set and $A={-20,-16,-12,-8,…,20},$ then $\\overset{―}{A}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351259 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "99c47e36-6326-59cd-8a70-c88572cc5f54" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351259 #edb/ref 1074 "The complement of $A,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{A},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $A.$\n\nThe universal set $U$ consists of the even integers $-20$ through $20,$ while the set $A$ consists of the multiples of $4$ from $-20$ through $20.$\n\nSo, the only elements of $U$ that are not in $A$ are the even integers from $-18$ through $18$ that are not multiples of $4.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $A$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{A}={-18,-14,-10,-6,-2,2,6,10,14,18}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351347 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186350742 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351347 #edb/ref 1069 "q-81695" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351347 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351347 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/3b/3b539190899ca580528fdbf7b5d3ef9925ade29f97f4b2f96b0f1394743f40a8.png)\n\nGiven the sets $S={p,a,s,w,o,r,d}$ and $T={p,o,r,t,e,l},$ find $T∖S.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351347 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "065e9298-e9b9-5450-a8e3-c9e554981a9b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351347 #edb/ref 1074 "The difference $T∖S$ consists of all the elements that are in $T$ but not $S.$ To represent $T∖S,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $T$ but not $S.$\n\n![](images/c7/c718918667c5076f8696ea98f453ff17f005d5f7cace87bd863be309fac28d72.png)\n\nThe elements $t,e,$ and $l$ are in $T$ but not $S.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nT∖S={t,e,l}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351367 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186350721 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351367 #edb/ref 1069 "q-81766" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351367 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351367 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $A$  be the set of all multiples of $3$ greater than $0$ and let $B$  be the set of all multiples of $4$ greater than $0.$ What is $B-A?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351367 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "08cc3802-c796-53b6-b40f-b3be60f49c05" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351367 #edb/ref 1074 "The multiples of $3$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nA={3,6,9,12,15,18,21,24,…}.\n$$\n\nLikewise, multiples of $4$ that are greater than $0$ are\n\n$$\nB={4,8,12,16,20,24,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, $B-A$ is the *difference* of $B$ and $A,$ which means that we want to find the elements that are in $B$ but *not* in $A.$\n\nThe elements of $B$ that are also in $A$ are $12,24,$ and so on (i.e. multiples of $12$). So, we must remove these elements from $B.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B-A & ={4,8,12,16,20,24,…}-{3,6,9,12,15,18,21,24,…} \\\\  & ={4,8,16,20,…}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351589 #edb/ref 1080 "{c,40}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351589 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351589 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "02b6103e-2899-5523-ac79-862e1c145ba0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921863