R?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354480 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4434ccc8-02d5-5a76-9c36-2b57d531d580" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354480 #edb/ref 1074 "The complement of $R,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{R},$ consists of all the elements in $U$ that are not in $R.$ To represent $\\overset{―}{R},$ we will shade in all the area of $U$ that is *outside* of $R,$ as follows:\n\n![](images/79/79900f22c35570b35cf10664768ecf4460a7953ddf7f91dac1893b3ce81339bf.png)\n\nThe elements in the shaded area are $a$ and $c.$ These are the elements of $U$ that are not in $R.$ Therefore, the complement of $R$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{R}={a,c}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354481 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186354100 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354481 #edb/ref 1069 "q-86590" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354481 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354481 #edb/ref 1071 "If $U={2,4,6,8,10,12}$ is the universal set and $B={2,6,10},$ then the complement of $B$ is" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354481 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "04125aec-6df3-511f-bf67-6f782ff92bbb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354481 #edb/ref 1074 "The complement of $B,$ denoted $\\overset{―}{B},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $B.$\n\nThe elements of $U$ that are not in $B$ are $4,$ $8,$   and $12.$\n\nTherefore, the complement of $B$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{B}={4,8,12}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354497 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186354073 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354497 #edb/ref 1069 "q-86701" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354497 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354497 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/96/96962d11526f30beee45b85aac92808518352d7b79b4b4f2e4a7351ddd9fe17e.png)\n\nGiven the sets $S={5,7,9}$ and $T={0,1,3},$find $S∖T.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354497 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "af7efa2c-3ffa-5821-9cbc-8c2275ebe689" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186354497 #edb/ref 1074 "The difference $S∖T$ consists of all the elements that are in $S$ but not $T.$ To represent $S∖T,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $S$ but not $T.$\n\n![](images/be/be1caefc99bea5d4dde0ba272a208dd8f587156029ce37df483e40cd5f6121d2.png)\n\nAll elements of $S$ are not in $T.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nS∖T={5,7,9}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399685 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186399686 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399685 #edb/ref 1069 "q-110078" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399685 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399685 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/39/3905dacc3977857933a48ced329fc245b357f732aec520e67998efc0b5d7cdab.png)\n\nWhich of the following systems of inequalities defines the shaded region shown above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399685 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b9a72356-7e05-5f10-b6ac-a2418c3b4fa6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399685 #edb/ref 1074 "Consider the line $x+2y=-8.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Writing the equation of this line in slope-intercept form, we have\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x-4.\n$$\n\nNow, since the shaded region lies *above* the line, the inequality is a \"greater than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\ge -\\frac{1}{2}x-4,\n$$\n\n    \n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\nx+2y\\ge -8.\n$$\n\nNow consider the line $y=\\frac{1}{2}x+1.$ Since the line is solid, the inequality is an \"or equal to\" inequality. Also, since the shaded region lies *below* the line, the inequality is a \"less than\" inequality. So the corresponding inequality is\n\n$$\ny\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the system of inequalities that defines the shaded region is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y\\ge -8 \\\\ y\\le \\frac{1}{2}x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399686 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186399687 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186399686 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 